<title>GERMANY: Albingia doubles 96 pre-tax profit.</title>
<headline>Albingia doubles 96 pre-tax profit.</headline>
<dateline>HAMBURG, Germany 1997-02-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Calendar 1996</p>
<p>(in millions of marks unless otherwise stated)</p>
<p>    Group pre-tax profit		     61.1	vs 30.0</p>
<p>    Group underwriting result		71.3 loss vs 85.5 loss</p>
<p>    Group financial result		   161.6     vs 139.5</p>
<p>NOTE - Full name of the German insurer is Albingia Versicherungs AG. All figures are provisional. The company also said in a mandatory statement that its gross premiums income fell slightly. The company also said it planned to raise its dividend by an &quot;appropriate&quot; amount, subject to shareholder approval on July 3. It paid a dividend of nine marks per common share and ten marks per preferred share in 1995.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
